ITEMS = ((('how do i dress a wound at home', 'what is the right way to dress a wound', 'how to put a dressing on a wound', 'what should i cover a wound with', 'how do you dress a small wound', 'what is the best dressing for a wound', 'steps for dressing a wound', 'how to bandage a wound properly', 'how can i dress a wound on my arm', 'what to do before dressing a wound'), 'To dress a wound, wash your hands, clean the area gently and pat it dry. Place a clean non-stick dressing over it and secure it without cutting off circulation. Ask a pharmacist or doctor if you are unsure about a deep or weeping wound.'), (('what type of dressing should i use for a wound', 'how do i choose a wound dressing', 'which dressing is best for a weeping wound', 'what dressings are available for wounds', 'should i use a non stick dressing', 'what is a hydrocolloid dressing for', 'how to pick a dressing for a scrape', 'what dressing suits a small wound', 'should i ask a pharmacist about wound dressings', 'what dressing stops a wound sticking'), 'The right dressing depends on how much the wound weeps and where it is. A non-stick pad suits many small wounds, while a hydrocolloid dressing can help shallow weeping ones. Ask a pharmacist to recommend a product for your particular wound.'), (('how often should i change a wound dressing', 'when to change the dressing on a wound', 'should i change a wound dressing every day', 'how long can a wound dressing stay on', 'what if a wound dressing falls off', 'should i change a wet dressing', 'how often to replace a dressing on a cut', 'when is it too soon to change a wound dressing', 'how to remove a wound dressing gently', 'what if a dressing sticks to the wound'), 'Change a wound dressing when it becomes wet, dirty or loose, and follow any advice given by a nurse or doctor for your wound type. Remove it gently and look for redness or discharge. Ask a healthcare professional if the wound looks worse after dressing changes.'), (('should i clean a wound before dressing it', 'how to clean around a wound dressing', 'what to put on a wound before covering it', 'do i need antiseptic before a dressing', 'how do i dry a wound before dressing', 'should i rinse a wound under the tap', 'what cleans a wound ready for a dressing', 'how to prepare a wound for a plaster', 'can i use soap on a wound before dressing', 'what is the reason to clean a wound first'), 'Rinse the wound with clean water and gently pat it dry before applying a dressing. Avoid scrubbing the raw area or using harsh products that delay healing. Ask a pharmacist about suitable cleansers, and get help if the wound looks deep or contaminated.'), (('how do i dress a weeping wound', 'what dressing is good for wound discharge', 'should i cover a wound that is weeping', 'how to manage fluid from a wound', 'what if a dressing soaks through', 'how to protect skin around a weeping wound', 'what kind of dressing absorbs wound fluid', 'is it bad to let a wound dry out', 'how often to change a dressing for discharge', 'when to get help for a weeping wound'), 'A weeping wound needs a dressing that absorbs fluid while keeping the wound bed moist. Change it when it becomes saturated and protect the surrounding skin from irritation. Ask a nurse or doctor if the discharge smells, changes colour or the redness spreads.'), (('can i shower with a wound dressing', 'how to keep a wound dressing dry', 'is a waterproof dressing good for wounds', 'what if water gets under a dressing', 'can i swim with a wound dressing', 'how to cover a wound when washing', 'should i remove a dressing before a shower', 'what happens if a wound plaster gets wet', 'how to protect a wound dressing at the gym', 'which wound dressings tolerate water'), 'Many modern dressings can be covered for a short shower, but check the packet or ask a pharmacist. If water gets underneath, change the dressing and dry the skin gently. Get advice if the wound becomes soggy, red or more painful after getting wet.'), (('what if i am allergic to wound dressings', 'can a plaster irritate my wound', 'what dressing is best for sensitive skin', 'my wound itches under the dressing', 'should i stop using a dressing that stings', 'what if tape causes a rash near a wound', 'how to avoid irritation from wound dressings', 'is there a dressing for delicate skin', 'what to use instead of adhesive wound plasters', 'when to ask about a dressing reaction'), 'If tape or a dressing makes the skin itchy or rashy, try a non-adhesive pad held with a soft bandage. Check the wound underneath and stop using anything that causes a reaction. Ask a pharmacist or doctor for a hypoallergenic option if irritation continues.'), (('how do i dress a wound on a joint', 'what dressing stays on a knee wound', 'how to bandage a wound on the elbow', 'should a wound dressing allow movement', 'what dressing works on a finger wound', 'how to keep a dressing on a moving area', 'how to dress a wound on the hand', 'what if a dressing restricts my movement', 'how to cover a wound on the ankle', 'when to get help dressing a wound on a joint'), 'Use a flexible dressing that moves with the joint and avoid wrapping so tightly that it restricts blood flow. Check that the area stays warm and feels normal. Ask a pharmacist for a secure product, or a doctor if the wound lies over a moving joint and keeps reopening.'), (('how to dress a wound that will not stop bleeding', 'what if a wound keeps bleeding through the dressing', 'should i add more dressings to a bleeding wound', 'when is a wound dressing not enough', 'what if a wound looks deeper after dressing', 'how to tell if a wound needs medical care', 'should i see a nurse for a wound dressing', 'what if the skin around a wound turns red', 'when to call emergency services for a wound', 'what if a dressed wound becomes very painful'), 'If bleeding soaks through a dressing, add another layer and keep applying pressure rather than removing the first one. Seek urgent medical help if bleeding continues, the wound is deep, or redness and pain spread. Call emergency services for heavy bleeding that will not slow.'), (('how do i remove a wound dressing safely', 'should i wash my hands before changing a wound dressing', 'what to do with a used wound dressing', 'how to store wound dressings at home', 'can i reuse a wound dressing', 'should i check the wound under the dressing', 'what if a wound dressing leaves marks on skin', 'how to keep spare wound dressings handy', 'when to ask a nurse about wound dressings', 'what to expect when a wound dressing is applied'), 'Clean hands and a clean surface help keep a wound dressing safe to use. Dispose of used dressings according to local guidance and keep unused ones dry and sealed. Ask a nurse or pharmacist if you need help choosing or changing a dressing.'))
